From 5b680adeafa2b4b1268659bec7f69e2c2ae5c1f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:09:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] planner.http: send presentation style as delimited user
 data; settle on pre-aborted signals

- The style is now a user-role message wrapped in <presentation_style> tags and
  labelled as data, never a system message, so a provider's text cannot carry
  system authority over the decision rules. A closing tag in the text is removed.
- resolvePresentationStyle returns at once when the combined signal is already
  aborted, and the abort promise re-checks after registering its listener (abort
  events are not replayed), so a provider that never settles cannot stall plan().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019yYfNBZEarUprrgszvBK49
